auditcore_auth 0.1.0 — attribution and authorization

New implementation in auditcore. The behaviour was characterised by executing
the password and JWT helpers of nine applications at pinned commits (listed
with the blob SHAs of every read file in provenance.json):
janpow77/audit_designer, flownavigator, flowsearch, qaaudit, versteigerung,
regulierung, flowinvoice, audit-portal and flowlib. Hash formats, claim
layouts, algorithms and lifetimes were adopted as compatibility profiles; the
code was rewritten. janpow77/cockpit and janpow77/riskanalysis were inspected
and contain no JWT or password hashing to adopt.

On 2026-09-22 the rights holder decided: "die Bibliotheken sollen MIT sein,
die anderen Repos nicht; die Bibliotheken kommen nach auditcore". On
2026-09-25 the rights holder asked to build auditcore_auth from group 1 of the
Python helper inventory. Status: USER_AUTHORIZED_MIT for this library only;
the applications keep their own licensing.

No third-party code is included. Optional extras use bcrypt (Apache-2.0),
argon2-cffi (MIT), PyJWT (MIT) and FastAPI (MIT) as ordinary dependencies.
